Binding the bone grid

125
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:26,000
Binding the bone grid is a part of the 3D modeling process that is used to create a bone structure made up of joints and bones,

126
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:28,000
so that the model object can be built.

127
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:34,000
In Everywhere, binding the bone grid will bind the clothing to the joints of the virtual model,

128
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:38,000
synchronizing their movement so that the clothing can be naturally moved along with the virtual model.

129
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:41,000
The binding process also includes the composition of the whole.

130
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:47,000
It defines the extent to which each part of the clothing is affected by the movement of the virtual model joints.

131
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:54,000
This creates an empty structure that allows the clothing and the virtual model to move smoothly together.

132
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:58,000
Although Colo and Marvelous Designer are focused on the fabric model of Bizhen,

133
00:08:58,000 --> 00:09:01,000
they are able to create lively clothing animations.

134
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:04,000
However, the size of the file is often larger due to the simulation of the animation,

135
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:08,000
resulting in lower efficiency in the game environment.

136
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:16,000
Therefore, in the game industry, the action of binding the bone grid is usually used in the same way as clothing and virtual models.

137
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:22,000
The Binding Bone Grid function of Everywhere provides an efficient solution for connecting clothing and virtual models.

