236
00:16:31,200 --> 00:16:33,200
Sculpt brush

237
00:16:33,200 --> 00:16:36,200
Next is the Sculpt brush.

238
00:16:36,200 --> 00:16:38,200
You can press the Ctrl key to add points.

239
00:16:38,200 --> 00:16:39,200
Switch to the right panel.

240
00:16:39,200 --> 00:16:41,200
Select the Sculpt brush mode.

241
00:16:41,200 --> 00:16:47,200
If there is a gap or overlap in the clothing, you can use the Sculpt brush to directly adjust its shape.

242
00:16:47,200 --> 00:16:50,200
The Sculpt brush has three combination modes.

243
00:16:50,200 --> 00:16:52,200
Capture, Smooth and Repair Gap.

244
00:16:52,200 --> 00:16:56,200
You can use Ctrl and Tab to switch.

245
00:16:56,200 --> 00:16:59,200
In addition, the brush property is the same as the full-weight brush.

246
00:16:59,200 --> 00:17:05,200
It allows you to adjust the strength, size, focal length and depth.

247
00:17:05,200 --> 00:17:08,200
Capture brush is used to pull out the clothing part that penetrates the virtual model.

248
00:17:08,200 --> 00:17:14,200
It allows you to adjust the color of the clothing part or the overlap layer of the moving surface.

249
00:17:14,200 --> 00:17:16,200
Click and drag the area you need.

250
00:17:16,200 --> 00:17:21,200
It will move accordingly and does not affect the full weight.

251
00:17:21,200 --> 00:17:28,200
Sculpt brush is used to optimize the surface of the clothing or to make it look more natural in areas that are flat and uneven.

252
00:17:28,200 --> 00:17:32,200
Click and drag the area you need to apply the brush.

253
00:17:32,200 --> 00:17:36,200
The surface will become smooth and match the surrounding shape.

254
00:17:36,200 --> 00:17:42,200
Repair Gap Brush is used to overlap the grid between the virtual model and the clothing or the clothing.

255
00:17:42,200 --> 00:17:46,200
It is difficult to repair with other brushes.

256
00:17:46,200 --> 00:17:49,200
Select the brush tool and then switch to the sculpt mode.

257
00:17:49,200 --> 00:17:52,200
Capture, Smooth and Repair Gap.

258
00:17:52,200 --> 00:17:55,200
Adjust the strength, size, focal length and depth.

259
00:17:55,200 --> 00:17:58,200
Click and drag the area you need to apply the brush to the model.

260
00:17:58,200 --> 00:18:05,200
Using the brush in this way will automatically correct the collision between the virtual model and the clothing or the clothing between each other.

261
00:18:05,200 --> 00:18:11,200
To change the position of the virtual model, check if there is a gap in the clothing or an incorrect follow-up area.

262
00:18:11,200 --> 00:18:17,200
Use the full weight brush and sculpt brush functions of the current channel to adjust to nature.

263
00:18:17,200 --> 00:18:24,200
After all bindings and adjustments are completed, click and drag the button to return to the Everywhere window.

