00:20:31,200 --> 00:20:36,200
Formatting

292
00:20:36,200 --> 00:20:39,200
Formatting is a function that generates a sticker,

293
00:20:39,200 --> 00:20:43,200
which is used to capture the details of high-resolution models after optimization.

294
00:20:43,200 --> 00:20:50,200
The reason for using low-resolution for formatting is that low-resolution files are smaller and more suitable for optimization.

295
00:20:50,200 --> 00:20:59,200
In addition, game engines, AR and other digital platforms are usually difficult to handle high-resolution.

296
00:20:59,200 --> 00:21:02,200
By using Everywhere's texture preparation,

297
00:21:02,200 --> 00:21:11,200
you can create high-resolution high-resolution models without the need to create high-resolution models alone by using only optimized low-resolution generated hair stickers and environmental light blocking stickers.

298
00:21:11,200 --> 00:21:18,200
Hair stickers are the texture stickers that are commonly used in games and other interactive platforms.

299
00:21:18,200 --> 00:21:26,200
They show the surface details of high-resolution models on the low-resolution model without increasing the number of multiple edges.

300
00:21:26,200 --> 00:21:27,200
Environmental light blocking stickers

301
00:21:27,200 --> 00:21:29,200
Environmental light blocking stickers are a form of high-resolution high-resolution models.

302
00:21:29,200 --> 00:21:36,200
They are used to track the light on the surface of 3D models to simulate indirect shadows.

303
00:21:36,200 --> 00:21:43,200
The dark areas represent the parts with less light and the bright areas represent the surface with sufficient light.

304
00:21:43,200 --> 00:21:48,200
These stickers can predict shadows and simulate the effect of indirect lighting around the environment,

305
00:21:48,200 --> 00:21:52,200
thereby enhancing the sense of reality.

306
00:21:52,200 --> 00:21:55,200
In Everywhere's texture preparation window,

307
00:21:55,200 --> 00:21:58,200
select the detail hair sticker and the environmental light blocking sticker.

308
00:21:58,200 --> 00:22:04,200
The environmental light blocking sticker's amount of light is the amount of light in each pixel.

309
00:22:04,200 --> 00:22:09,200
The higher the value, the more accurate the result, but it will increase the calculation time.

310
00:22:09,200 --> 00:22:16,200
After setting the configuration, click the application button to generate a sticker.

311
00:22:16,200 --> 00:22:21,200
Click the preview button to view the prepared stickers in the 3D window.

312
00:22:21,200 --> 00:22:27,200
The strength of the sticker can be found by entering the value or adjusting it with the slider in the strength bar.

313
00:22:28,200 --> 00:22:33,200
The default value is 100, and the setting range is from 0 to 200.

314
00:22:33,200 --> 00:22:39,200
If you want to delete the generated stickers, click the trash can icon.

315
00:22:39,200 --> 00:22:44,200
